  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening communities in human-tiger conflict (HTC) sensitive Dhela forest range of the Corbett Tiger Reserve, India through income generating development skill training, alternative cooking fuel</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen the capacity of the local villagers around the Corbett Tiger Reserve (CTR) through community livelihood improvement and income generating skill development training program, and help them develop positive understanding and appreciation for wildlife, and coordinate with the Forest Department to reduce human tiger/wildlife conflicts and deforestation. The project objectives are as follows: (1) Build a Community Livelihood Improvement (CLI) Training Center (CLITC) for the human-tiger conflict (HTC) affected womens communities in Dhela forest range of the CTR; (2) Provide income generating skill development training in the CLITC to the forest-dependent women stakeholders of Dhela forest range; (3) Provide alternative cooking fuel and cooking gas subsidy to the human-tiger conflict affected families in the Dhela forest range; (4) Build the capacity of the frontline forest staff working at the forest check posts in Dhela forest range; (5) Initiate developing a Community Plant Nursery as a measure to promote community-led tiger habitat protection in Dhela forest range; (6) Propagate HTC mitigation awareness education campaign in the HTC sensitive villages around the CTR.</narrative>
  </description>
